692:I understand.
693:Well, this wouldn't be a problem if the reporter who follows you is someone who you and Miss Mikami already know, right?
696:Wait! Hold on! Are you both thinking what I'm thinking?
698:In the end, I was given the important task of following and filming Riu Kujou for one day.
699:Correspondingly, since Chihori Terasaki wouldn't be able to get one of her reporters to follow and film Riu Kujou, she proposed that she would decide whether to give Riu Kujou the teddy bear after reviewing the quality of the filmed content.
701:Yes...
703:Everything is difficult at the beginning. Stick with it for the teddy bear, Riu!
705:Okay!
706:I adjust the machine and start filming again.
709:Riu Kujou's face is still bright red, so we can't continue filming anymore, and my head starts to hurt when I look at the lines prepared for the interview. How should I go about this now?
711:Insist on trying a few more times because practice makes perfect
713:Suggest filming another part first
714:We won't get anywhere if we keep wasting time like this. We should try something else if this isn't working.
715:Let's film this part later.
717:Riu Kujou breathes an obvious sigh of relief and glances at the time.
718:I was starting to worry that we would spend the entire morning doing this and wouldn't be able to complete the work I had scheduled.
719:If we do that, we really will lose sight of everything else for this. Just pretend that I don't exist from now on and focus on what you need to do. I'll be responsible for filming some good stuff.
721:Riu Kujou pats my shoulder sincerely and earnestly.
722:Umm, I'll just be filming you. It's not hard work. Please start doing your work now.
723:The first thing she'll do is the laundry for her lady? Exceptional cleaning abilities are a key trait of a good maid, so I must film this.
728:Riu Kujou looks worriedly at me who is about to put down the action camera and sit down.
731:Half an hour later, I'm leaning against a shelf in a supermarket with a full shopping cart, while Riu Kujou is still picking products not far from me. I put down the action camera and rub my sore arms.
734:That's what I felt the first time I met Miss Kujou, but she seems to be managing things well over these years.
736:I turn my head and see Sawako Kitami standing next to me behind a shopping cart, and she is looking at us with raised eyebrows. I have no idea when she got here.
737:Sawako Kitami
738:It's such a coincidence. I came over to say hi because I saw Miss Kujou and wasn't expecting to see you here.
740:Yes, we got to know each other because we often go to the same supermarket, choose foods together, and share recipes with each other.
741:I see.
742:I must admit that One Han City is a really small place sometimes.
743:So what are you filming? Something like a vlog?
745:I tell her what we're doing.
747:Hmm? I can't wait.
749:When she finally gave it to the children to try, they pointed at the bear sushi that she spent a lot of time making and said, "These piglets are so cute." Miss Kujou was depressed for quite some time after that.
753:Oh, there you are, Miss Kujou. I was just telling {var:player_nickname} cute stories about you. Your interview will definitely be a smashing success.
755:Hmm? Okay, let's go.
757:Hmm?
759:After receiving a sharp glare from Riu Kujou, I put away my dangerous curiosity.
761:Chiori Mikami's House
762:No, you have to eat everything.
763:But isn't this too much food?
764:I look at the two large plates of salmon in front of me that are basically untouched as I complain weakly.
765:I ended up buying so much food to attract Ms. Kitami's attention because you were filming all sorts of strange things in the supermarket just now. That's why you have to eat everything while it's fresh.
767:I rub my bulging belly and find myself really missing Ichihime right now. Sigh, I should have brought her with me today.
768:Anyway, I'm leaving all of this to you. Let's stop filming for today.
771:You can find a place to play mahjong in the afternoon. You can come over and film the self-introduction later.
773:I take some time to look at the interview outline, and it really doesn't say that we need to film Riu's personal activities. On that day, all Chihori Terasaki said was that we should film content that viewers would be interested in watching.
775:Keep filming Riu Kujou
776:Play mahjong
778:Riu, can I keep you company during your personal time in the afternoon?
779:Huh? Are you sure you want to film me when I'm not working as a maid? The interview guidelines don't say anything about that though. I already feel bad about making you help me, so isn't it better to avoid unnecessary work?
781:I don't know about anyone else, but if I'm a reader, if I'm watching this interview, I'll be watching it because I want to know what Riu Kujou is like when she isn't working as a maid.
784:At least that's what I think.
786:Sure!
787:The first thing I do after finishing my work is to do some daily physical exercise here.
789:To my surprise, the first place Riu Kujou takes me to is a Taekwondo dojo, and I'm completely astonished to see a photo of Riu Kujou wearing a Taekwondo dobok and beating her opponent to the ground on the wall of the dojo.
791:In other words, you're stronger than your dan indicates, right...
793:After doing some physical exercise, I usually take a stroll and buy whatever catches my eye along the way.
795:For example, I might go to the tailor shop to buy fabric to make a beautiful dress for Miss Chiori, I might go to a household goods store to look for new housekeeping tools, or I might go to the bookstore to search for more useful schedule planners, new cookbooks, recent best-selling organization guides, etc.
796:Most girls don't go shopping for these things!
798:Fully satisfied with a bag full of fabrics, daily necessities, and books, Riu Kujou suddenly stops walking.
799:Hmm? Is it time to go back?
801:I follow Riu Kujou's gaze and see a tea house next to a road.
803:Well, I only learned how to make tea before because it's a basic skill of a maid. I only started to really pay attention to the tea ceremony after chatting with my teacher about the tea ceremony at the Mahjong Soul Shrine last time.
807:Haha, thanks!
808:Ah, my bag! Help! There's a thief!
809:Suddenly, an urgent shout stops us in our tracks, and a figure runs past us quickly. Before I can react, Riu Kujou's bursting shopping bag suddenly appears in my hand, and she is already chasing after the figure.
810:I quickly grab my action camera and chase after them. After passing an intersection, I arrive just in time to see Riu Kujou kick the thief to the ground with a horizontal kick.
811:There are gasps of surprise all around us.
